    "result_text": "Both tests pass. Here's what I implemented as a full-stack change for \"an invoice amount must be more than zero\":\n\n**Front-end** (`features/invoices/InvoiceForm.tsx`) \u2014 the form previously rejected a non-positive amount *silently* (just returned). I added a transient `error` state (local `useState`, since it belongs to the uncommitted field the user is editing) that renders a `data-testid=\"invoice-form-amount-error\"` message on a zero/negative/empty submit and clears when they edit the field. A valid amount still submits and adds the row.\n\n**Server** \u2014 `InvoicesPostLogic` already validated `amount.signum() <= 0` \u2192 400, so no change was needed there; it remains the request-level line of defence.\n\n**Database** (`db/migration/V6__invoices_amount_positive.sql`) \u2014 a new Flyway migration adding a `CHECK (amount > 0)` constraint, mirroring the existing V2 email-format pattern so a bad row can't slip in through any path.\n\nThe two features (form, list) still share only the `['invoices', projectId]` query key \u2014 no cross-imports, no edits to pinned scaffolding. Frontend typecheck and both Playwright tests (`@error` reject, `@core` accept) pass.",
